   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The overlap matrix shows whether neighboring umbrella windows form a connected sampling network. Stronger off-diagonal overlap means that configurations sampled in one state also carry appreciable statistical weight in another. Weak overlap identifies regions where free-energy estimates are expected to become more sensitive to sampling noise and where a chained Zwanzig calculation is particularly vulnerable to accumulated uncertainty.\n"
   ]
  },
